RF.put("questb:b5",{"8565":{"id":8565,"t":"Past Victories in Arathi","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Arathi Resource Crate","desc":"Ah, yes! Of course we wouldn't forget about your past accomplishments in Arathi Basin.","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Arathi Basin Mark of Honor\nLevel 1 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 4 6 Side Alliance Shareable Yes Quest ID 8565","cats":["arathi-basin"]},"645":{"id":645,"t":"Trol'kalar","lv":42,"min":32,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve Trol'kalar from Trollbane's tomb in Stromgarde.\nSigil of Ignaeus\nProvided: Sigil of Ignaeus","desc":"What's this? With the four sigils brought together, they have formed together to create one sigil. There can be no doubt that this will be able to break the wardings placed upon Trollbane's tomb.\nTrollbane's remains are entombed in the Sanctum behind the chapel in Stromgarde. Retrieve Trol'kalar.","rew":"Experience: 850\n+25 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Etchings in the stone upon the face of the tomb of Trollbane match the glowing lines of the Sigil of Ignaeus...","done":"Matching the lines on the face of Trollbane's tomb with the glowing lines of the Sigil of Ignaeus, a flash of light consumes the Sigil, and the legendary sword Trol'kalar is released from the stone hands' grip.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":73.8,"y":34,"n":"Zengu","s":1},{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":28.9,"y":59.6,"n":"Trollbane's Tomb","e":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"1045":{"id":1045,"t":"Raene's Cleansing","lv":30,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 4 Bloodtooth Guards and retrieve Ran Bloodtooth's Skull for Krolg near Lake Mystral.\nBloodtooth Guard slain : 0/ 4\nRan Bloodtooth's Skull\nProvided: Dartol's Rod of Transformation","desc":"The night elves are as old as time, but their arrogance destroys their very world. And now it destroys our lives too. But that can no longer be controlled...\nI blame the elves for much, but we are still responsible for our actions. Even beyond the corruption, we are capable of great evil.\nRan Bloodtooth is one such evil. Power hungry, lusting... the corruption has only made him stronger. My hatred for the elves burns, but I do not wish ill upon their children, so we must police our own.","rew":"Experience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"Have you slain Ran yet, my friend?\nEven the Night elves do not truly deserve his wrath. His hatred burns even brighter than my own, but his mind is no longer his own. He is a threat to all the natural creatures of this forest.","done":"You have done well, my friend.\nThe forest is still tainted, but at least we know we have done a small part to return it to its former glory. If you wish to return to me again, I would enjoy the company of my own kind.\nBe well. Perhaps our tribes will meet again under less violent times.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":50.8,"y":75.1,"n":"Krolg","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"6805":{"id":6805,"t":"Stormers and Rumblers","lv":57,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 15 Dust Stormers and 15 Desert Rumblers and then return to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.\nDust Stormer slain : 0/ 15\nDesert Rumbler slain : 0/ 15","desc":"We, the elementals of water, wage war with those beings of the lesser elements. If you are truly our ally in this conflict, then show me your conviction!\nFar to the south, in the desert land of Silithus, the servants of air and earth scurry in a corner of rock named the Crystal Vale. They protect items of power from smaller beings, mortals, and although I do not know why they do this, I wish to foil their efforts.\nGo to the Crystal Vale in Silithus and defeat our enemies, then return to me.","rew":"Experience: 6,000","back":"Cowardice is not a thing we hold in regard, ‹class›. Go to Silithus and prove your bravery.","done":"Your bravery is proven, as is your worth to us. Perhaps I may have future tasks for you, tasks more befitting a valued ally of the Waterlords.\nAzshara Silithus","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":79.3,"y":73.7,"n":"Duke Hydraxis","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["azshara"]},"725":{"id":725,"t":"Passing Word of a Threat","lv":40,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Advisor Belgrum and give him his note.\nSealed Note to Advisor Belgrum\nProvided: Sealed Note to Advisor Belgrum","desc":"‹name›, run and find Advisor Belgrum as quickly as you can. Tell him what you've witnessed and ask him how he wants us to proceed. This note will explain more to him.\nIn the meantime, I will take the time to speak to Hammertoe's spirit. Maybe he knows something that will help us put a stop to those Shadowforge cretins' activities in the Badlands. We can only pray.","rew":"Experience: 1,550\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Hmm? Yes, ‹class›.","done":"Ah, word from Historian Karnik. Excellent.\nI always have time for his business.\n<Advisor Belgrum opens the note and begins to read.>","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":23,"n":"Historian Karnik","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":22.6,"n":"Advisor Belgrum","e":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"6565":{"id":6565,"t":"Allegiance to the Old Gods","lv":26,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,300 experience instead of 2,650, 2.38 times as much. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Kill Lorgus Jett in Blackfathom Deeps and then return to Je'neu Sancrea in Ashenvale.\nLorgus Jett slain","desc":"This Twilight's Hammer follower cannot be allowed to complete his plan. The Twilight's Hammer do not understand the spirits of nature. They believe in the Old Gods--creatures of chaos and destruction that were long ago defeated. This Lorgus cannot be allowed to succeed. You must stop him, ‹name›. I cannot do it myself--I am too weak.\nGo into Blackfathom Deeps, find him, and kill him. Return to me here at Zoram'gar when it's done.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nBand of the Fist Chestnut Mantle\nMoney: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,300\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls\n+150 reputation with Earthen Ring","back":"Have you found him yet, ‹name›? Lorgus must be stopped!","done":"Very good!! Thank you, ‹name›. We may not have stopped the Twilight's Hammer completely, but at least you have staved off another of their plans to return the Old Gods to power.\nWho knows what other plans they have manifesting, but we can rest easy for now.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":11.6,"y":34.3,"n":"Je'neu Sancrea","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackfathom-deeps"]},"8965":{"id":8965,"t":"Components of Importance","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Obtain Soul Ashes of the Banished and return them to Bodley inside Blackrock Mountain.\nSoul Ashes of the Banished Writhing Mage , Cursed Justicar , Cursed Paladin","desc":"‹class›, listen closely. Now that we have the brazier, and the means to light it, we still need another component to suffuse it with; something that will provide a focus strong enough to entice the spirit of my deceased, former comrade.\nAn ogre necromancer that traveled with us, Kormok, delighted in summoning forth the souls of the banished dead of Purgation Isle, off the south coast of the Hillsbrad Foothills. Go there and retrieve some Soul Ashes of the Banished from their remains.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Have you returned already then, ‹class›, with what I sent you out to gather?","done":"A job well done, ‹name›. I will imbue the essence of the ashes into the brazier.\nNow all that is left is to get into Scholomance, to Ras Frostwhisper's chamber, and use the brazier to summon forth the spirit of my former cohort, Kormok. The amulet piece, and Valthalak's spirit within, has corrupted him even further, and he will not rest until you forcibly take it from him.\nBurning Steppes Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":32.3,"y":25.8,"n":"Bodley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"97925":{"id":97925,"t":"Camping 101 tailoring","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Eldrin in the Eastvale Logging Camp in Elwynn Forest to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your tailoring skill to 20","desc":"Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":79.2,"y":69,"n":"Eldrin","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94245":{"id":94245,"t":"Craftsmans writ barbaric gloves","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Barbaric Gloves\nBarbaric Gloves","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Barbaric Gloves, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Barbaric Gloves Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94245","cats":["crafting"]},"94325":{"id":94325,"t":"Craftsmans writ radiant circlet","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Radiant Circlet\nRadiant Circlet","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Radiant Circlet, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Radiant Circlet Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94325","cats":["crafting"]},"4725":{"id":4725,"t":"Beached Sea Turtle","lv":15,"min":12,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Strangely Marked Box to Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine.\nStrangely Marked Box\nProvided: Strangely Marked Box","desc":"More sea turtle remains lie beached along the coastline. This particular set has an abandoned carriage attached to the turtle's shell. Perhaps this creature was driven to the shoreline by unknown beings rather than beaching itself as some of the other remains suggested. Greymist murlocs now make the remains of this creature their home, feasting off the carrion.\nIn the carriage, you find a box with strange markings on it; perhaps Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde in Auberdine can make sense of it.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 550\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","back":"It is a pleasure to see you again, ‹name›. We are making great strives in uncovering the mystery of why majestic sea creatures beach themselves on the Darkshore coastline, but with every question answered, two more are raised it seems.\nAre you here to offer us more aid in our research?","done":"I have heard of the kinds of carriages found on the back of the turtle you found. Those I do believe are naga carriages, used both in battle and in transportation of their supplies on to land. The markings on the box you found are of the naga; this would explain their invasive presence in far-northern Darkshore.\nI will send this box to Darnassus along with the rest of your discoveries. This is for you - thank you again for your assistance.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":44.2,"y":20.6,"n":"Beached Sea Turtle","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":36.6,"y":45.6,"n":"Gwennyth Bly'Leggonde","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"965":{"id":965,"t":"The Tower of Althalaxx","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Balthule Shadowstrike near the Tower of Althalaxx in Darkshore.","desc":"Hail, young ‹race›. I am Elissa Starbreeze, and it is my charge to protect Auberdine from harm.\nTo this end, I sent Balthule Shadowstrike to observe the strange happenings around the Tower of Althalaxx to the northeast.\nIt is past time that he should have returned. I worry that he has encountered some unforeseen danger in the forest. I would be most appreciative if you would find him and see that he is doing well.","rew":"Experience: 675\n+50 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Elissa sent you? Then it is good tidings you bring. I have troubling news to report to her, and had no means with which to deliver it.","pins":[{"z":"Darkshore","x":39,"y":43.6,"n":"Sentinel Elissa Starbreeze","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":55,"y":24.9,"n":"Balthule Shadowstrike","e":1}],"cats":["darkshore"]},"1365":{"id":1365,"t":"Khan Dez'hepah","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Khan Dez'hepah's Head to Felgur Twocuts in Desolace.\nKhan Dez'hepah's Head Khan Dez'hepah","desc":"The Kolkar are not the only centaur of Desolace. Many clans wander these dry plains, fighting and dying against each other. And it is good that they fight among themselves, for they are strong and brutal. If the centaur united against us, they would be a fierce foe.\nWe must deal with them before they unite.\nYour first task is to disrupt the Kolkar clan. Do this by killing its leader, Khan Dez'hepah.\nThe Kolkar Village is northeast of here. Go, and may fortune go with you.","rew":"Experience: 3,450\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"‹name›, have you defeated Khan Dez'hepah?","done":"Well done. This swift act against the Kolkar is an effective show of strength, and strength is what the centaur understand best.\nThe death of the Kolkar leader will not only disrupt that clan, but give pause to the others.","pins":[{"z":"Desolace","x":56.2,"y":59.6,"n":"Felgur Twocuts","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["desolace"]},"93045":{"id":93045,"t":"Test your theory","lv":38,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and dispel the necromantic curse present on the Accursed Skull. Once successful, report back to Nerlokh near the Valley of Bones.\nUthek's Draenethyst Staff\nDispel the Accursed Skull\nGelkis Clan Centaur\nUthek's Staff","desc":"I have placed the skull you provided alongside several bones I found while awaiting your return. Immediately I saw a sickly light spread from the skull and claim those old bones as its own. I see now why the call of necromancy is so hard to resist.\nDo you remember this crystal? It is draenethyst. I know little of its potential, but I believe it can channel Theradras' power. With it, perhaps you can dispel the curse.\nThe ritual site can be found by the pond just east of the village.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCentaur Spear Wanderer's Broadsword Desert Crawler's Claw\nExperience: 700\n+500 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\nLevel 38 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 36 41 48 Side Both factions Quest ID 93045\nThe chain\n10 quests from level 32 to 38, 14,740 XP in all.\n1 [ 35 ] Strange Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nCaptain Pentigast Desolace\n2,050 XP\n2 [ 32 ] Raid on the Kolkar\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring 10 Crude Charms to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n2,550 XP\n[ 33 ] Gelkis Alliance\nGain a Friendly reputation with the Gelkis, then speak with Uthek the Wise.\nGurda Wildmane Desolace\n650 XP\n3 [ 35 ] Stealing Supplies\nBring 6 bags of Crudely Dried Meat to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n1,350 XP\n4 [ 37 ] Ongeku\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring a Draenethyst Shard to Uthek the Wise in the Gelkis Village in Desolace.\nUthek the Wise Desolace\n2,850 XP\n5 [ 38 ] Valley of Bones\nImprove your reputation with the Gelkis, and locate Nerlokh near the Valley of Bones far east of Gelkis Village.\n290 XP\n6 [ 38 ] Ravaging Ravagers\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan and slay 6 Undead Ravagers, then return to Nerlokh at the southern entrance to Valley of Bones.\n1,450 XP\n7 [ 38 ] Facing the Truth\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis Clan, and bring an Accursed Skull and Gelkis Necromantic Garb to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\n700 XP\n8 [ 38 ] A Cleansing Cry\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and bring Tears of Theradras back to Uthek the Wise in Gelkis Village.\n2,150 XP\n9 [ 38 ] Test Your Theory this quest\nMaintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and dispel the necromantic curse present on the Accursed Skull.\n700 XP","cats":["desolace"]},"5525":{"id":5525,"t":"Free Knot!","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 56 instead of 57.","obj":"Gordok Shackle Key Gordok Bushwacker 24.5 % , Guard Fengus 13 % , Guard Slip'kik 13 % , Captain Kromcrush 13 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","back":"It's called the Gordok Shackle Key - well, that's what these \"tons o' fun\" keep calling it. I think any of the ogres might have it, but I'm not sure if any specific ones do. Maybe the guards have a better chance of having one...\nWhat am I talking about - you have it already, don't you?! Is that it there??!","done":"Oh, thank you for freeing me! You - ranked number one. Everyone else - ranked number two or lower.\nI knew my life was destined for more than just being an appetizer to some ogre!\nStart Knot Thimblejack End Knot Thimblejack Level 60 , requires level 56 Difficulty 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 5525\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 7,250 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Free Knot! this quest\nKnot Thimblejack\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Free Knot!\nKnot Thimblejack\n650 XP","cats":["dire-maul"]},"92485":{"id":92485,"t":"A student of nature","lv":2,"min":2,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Read the Folded Parchment then speak with Xyton Silverwind in Thendal Grove.\nProvided: Folded Parchment","desc":"While you were away dealing with our vuldren problem, our resident druid trainer--Xyton Silverwind--left this note for you. Read it as soon as you can, and then seek out Silverwind on the ground floor of this great tree just behind me.\nHeed his words and his counsel, he can teach you much.","back":"Greetings, I am Xyton Silverwind, keeper of druidic lore.","done":"The flora and fauna of Zephras Isle represent a rich tapestry of vibrant life. The ecosystem requires constant balance to maintain the harmony of nature, and we druids are the keepers of that balance. I see much potential in you, but this path is not an easy one, and you will need guidance as you grow in strength as a student of the fang, the claw, the feather, and the branch.\nSpeak with me again if you wish to take your next steps.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42,"y":23.4,"n":"Rorian the Dayseeker","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":23.4,"n":"Xyton Silverwind","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"5925":{"id":5925,"t":"Heeding the Call","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Mathrengyl Bearwalker in the Cenarion Enclave, Darnassus.","desc":"Excuse me, friend...\nIt has come to my attention that Mathrengyl Bearwalker has put out word that he wishes to speak with you. It seems that your training as a druid is about to take on a new life, and he will be training you personally. Mathrengyl is the direct assistant to the Arch Druid himself, and is one of the most sage and august druids you'll find in Teldrassil.\nHe is located in the Cenarion Enclave of Darnassus, on the second floor of Fandral Staghelm's tree.","rew":"Experience: 85\n+25 reputation with Cenarion Circle","done":"I am glad you found your way here today. young ‹class›. The time has come for you to take a large step into a much larger world.\nInside each of Cenarius' children is the call to serve nature. Animals and plants are our friends as well as our charges. We choose to devote our lives as preservers of balance for their sakes as well as our own. Your first step into this world will be to learn of the ways of the bear, and to learn strength of body and heart.\nReady yourself!","pins":[{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":7.4,"n":"Denatharion","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":35.4,"y":8.4,"n":"Mathrengyl Bearwalker","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"98405":{"id":98405,"t":"The great cat spirit","lv":20,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Seek out the Great Cat Spirit in southern part Moonglade and learn what it has to share with you about the nature of the cat.","desc":"In the southern part of Moonglade, on a hill overlooking the bridge, resides a wise and cunning being we call the Great Cat Spirit.\nMuch like the Great Bear Spirit, this spirit has served as a tutor and mentor to druids that desire to take the feline shape. All druids eventually seek its wisdom, and if you desire to take the form of a cat, you will as well.\nGo meet with the Great Cat Spirit and learn what it will teach you.","done":"I see you have come to learn to draw upon my spirit. Good. Let us see if you are ready to take my shape.","pins":[{"z":"Moonglade","x":56.2,"y":30.4,"n":"Dendrite Starblaze","s":1},{"z":"Moonglade","x":54.6,"y":75,"n":"Great Cat Spirit","e":1}],"cats":["druid"]},"3365":{"id":3365,"t":"Bring Back the Mug","lv":5,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return Nori's Mug to Nori Pridedrift.\nNori's Mug\nProvided: Nori's Mug","desc":"Now that hit the spot! Nothing like a piping hot - nay, SCALDING mornbrew on a cold winter's day to warm your cackles of yer soul.\nHere ya go ‹name› - be a pal and take this empty mug back to Nori for me, would ya now.","rew":"Money: 50 0 gold, 0 silver, 50 copper Experience: 450\n+100 reputation with Ironforge\n+100 reputation with Gnomeregan Exiles","back":"I trust the scalding mornbrew got to Durnan on time! Did you remember to bring me back my mug?","done":"Excellent, ‹name›! You'd be surprised how many couriers I meet who forget to do something as simple as bring back the mug. Mugs don't grow on trees, or so they tell me!\nHere's a little something for the effort. Thanks again for your help.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.8,"y":66.4,"n":"Durnan Furcutter","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":25,"y":76,"n":"Nori Pridedrift","e":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"805":{"id":805,"t":"Report to Sen'jin Village","lv":5,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Master Gadrin in Sen'jin Village.","desc":"Your trials against the Burning Blade are finished... here in the Valley. But I want you to report your findings.\nGo to the troll village of Sen'jin and seek out Master Gadrin. Sen'jin Village is east out of the valley, then right at the fork.\nTell Gadrin of the Burning Blade, and that they have reached the Valley of Trials. Discover from him if they have yet reached Sen'jin.\nGo, ‹name›, and be swift. I fear the evil found in the Burning Blade Coven is but the herald of a larger threat...","rew":"Experience: 230\n+50 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+50 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","done":"Hm... your report comes at a bad time. The Burning Blade is not seen here in Sen'jin, but their evil has taken seed off the coast, on the Echo Isles.\nThe orcs are friends of the Darkspear Trolls. Honorable friends. We want to help the orcs, but... we need help too.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":42.8,"y":69.1,"n":"Zureetha Fargaze","s":1},{"z":"Durotar","x":55.9,"y":74.7,"n":"Master Gadrin","e":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"5":{"id":5,"t":"Jitters' Growling Gut","lv":20,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Chef Grual.","desc":"I've been stuck hiding in this ghost town for weeks, and I haven't eaten anything but grubs and weeds! I need some decent food, and I'm willing to trade well for it.\nBring me a feast and I'll pay you handsomely.\nI heard Chef Grual at the Scarlet Raven Tavern in Darkshire makes very good Dusky Crab Cakes...","rew":"Experience: 390\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"You need some Crab Cakes, do you? Well I might be able to cook some up for you...","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":18.4,"y":56.4,"n":"Jitters","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.8,"y":43.5,"n":"Chef Grual","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"245":{"id":245,"t":"Eight-Legged Menaces","lv":21,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 15 Pygmy Venom Web Spiders, and then report back to Watcher Dodds in Duskwood.\nPygmy Venom Web Spider slain : 0/ 15","desc":"Hail, ‹class›. Perhaps you've seen those spiders that have taken over the western border? The eight-legged menaces are too much for us to handle, and the Commander hasn't enough manpower to spare so far from Darkshire.\nI hate to ask this of you, but you seem like you might be able to handle them. I can't promise you anything of great value, but I can reward you if you can help root out the filthy bugs.\nOh, and a word of advice, you'll want to avoid their venom if you can.","rew":"You will receive:\nNight Watch Gauntlets\nExperience: 1,250\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You'd best be careful when dealing with the spiders, I've lost a few of my men to them, and trust me, it isn't a pleasant sight to see a man hanging upside down in their webs after the venom has started to soften them up.\nI wouldn't want to see one of the bugs having you for lunch.","done":"Ah! You're back. And not too much worse for wear, it'd seem. Of course, ‹name›, the Night Watch is grateful for your work, and I did promise you a reward, so here.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":45.1,"y":67,"n":"Watcher Dodds","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"165":{"id":165,"t":"The Hermit","lv":25,"min":17,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Check on the old man in the shack near Raven Hill cemetery.","desc":"There was an old man who used to come into town to buy supplies rather frequently, but I haven't seen him for quite some time now. He lives out in a shack overlooking Raven Hill cemetery, if I remember correctly. Perhaps you should go see if something is amiss.","rew":"Experience: 1,000\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Hehe, oh yes... of course, the Carevins.\nNo, nothing's wrong but it is hard for me to go into town now. The roads are dangerous and I'm not getting any younger. Maybe you can do an old man some favors?","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.3,"y":48.7,"n":"Elaine Carevin","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":28.1,"y":31.5,"n":"Abercrombie","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"325":{"id":325,"t":"Armed and Ready","lv":29,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Morbent's Bane to Sven in Duskwood.\nMorbent's Bane\nProvided: Morbent's Bane","desc":"Here is the weapon against the fiend of which you spoke. You're all ready, ‹name›. Best of luck to you, and I look forward to your tale of glory!","rew":"Experience: 600\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Hello, ‹name›. You haven't been gone that long, but I see a fire in your eyes I did not see before.","done":"Ah, this will be proof against the fiend Morbent Fel! Well done!\nYou are ready. Morbent Fel will fall.\nStormwind City Duskwood","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":59.7,"y":33.8,"n":"Grimand Elmore","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":7.8,"y":34.1,"n":"Sven Yorgen","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1285":{"id":1285,"t":"Daelin's Men","lv":38,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return the information about Reethe to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.","desc":"Reddon... Redpath... Ah, here it is! Lieutenant Paval Reethe.\nJoined the Theramore guard along with most of the recruits that came across the sea with Lady Proudmoore. Enlisted with the marines of Kul Tiras at the age of sixteen. Distinguished service, promotions...\nListed as missing.","rew":"Experience: 290","done":"Missing? That would be Tesoran's kind way of saying traitor.\nNo doubt he's one of those fools so blindly loyal to Admiral Daelin that he turned traitor. Isn't that a delicious irony? The deserters accuse us of betraying the Alliance.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68,"y":48.1,"n":"Adjutant Tesoran","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Captain Garran Vimes","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"1205":{"id":1205,"t":"Deadmire","lv":45,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Deadmire's Tooth to Melor in Thunder Bluff.\nDeadmire's Tooth Deadmire","desc":"Deadmire is an ancient crocolisk in Dustwallow marsh. And it is his time to die.\nOld bones grind as he pulls his huge body through the swamp, and although he still moves with the strength and speed of youth, his aging body tortures the great spirit within it, a spirit whose flame will not waver.\nYet now he lives in constant, maddening pain. You must end the life of this noble creature, ‹name›. You must lead Deadmire to peace.","rew":"Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"Do you have the tooth of Deadmire, ‹name›? Have you ended the creature's suffering?","done":"Very good, ‹name›.\nI am sure the hunt was not easy, but it is good to know the beast's pain has finally ended.\nThunder Bluff Dustwallow Marsh","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":61.5,"y":80.9,"n":"Melor Stonehoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"5845":{"id":5845,"t":"Of Lost Honor","lv":58,"min":52,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Northdale, in the northeastern region of the Eastern Plaguelands, and recover the Symbol of Lost Honor. Return to Tirion Fordring upon completion of your objective.\nSymbol of Lost Honor Symbol of Lost Honor","desc":"The Order of the Silver Hand was utterly decimated when Uther was slain.\nThe boy held out for as long as he could. Pushed to the war torn hamlet of Northdale, he made his final stand.\nWere any of the Order left alive, he thought - and did it matter?\nIt was with that thought that Taelan threw down the standard of the Order and renounced all that he had known. His honor left upon the blood soaked ground of Northdale.\nYou must travel to Northdale and recover that symbol of lost honor.","rew":"Experience: 6,200","back":"My faith will guide you, ‹name›. The Light knows no bounds.","done":"It is as glorious now - even in its tattered state - as the day I looked upon it and took my oath of allegiance.\nHis redemption comes and perhaps mine with it...","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":5.2,"y":35.6,"n":"Tirion Fordring","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9205":{"id":9205,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Plated Armorfish","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 30 Plated Armorfish and the Craftsman's Writ - Plated Armorfish - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\n30 Raw Plated Armorfish\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Plated Armorfish","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order FS-12:\n30 Plated Armorfish.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"You really don't know what these are for?\n<Packmaster Stonebruiser laughs.>\nLike I'm going to tell you!","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"9125":{"id":9125,"t":"Crypt Fiend Parts","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"30 Crypt Fiend Parts Nerubian Overseer , Necrofiend 79.1 % in Scholomance , Crypt Crawler 69.6 % in Stratholme , Crypt Beast 69.5 % in Stratholme and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\nInsignia of the Crusade\nMoney: 9 0 gold, 9 silver, 0 copper\n+10 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You did an exemplary job on the first bundle, ‹name›. If you have more, I will take them now. For every bundle that you turn in, I will reward you with another insignia.","done":"Most excellent, ‹name›! These will definitely come to good use.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.9,"n":"Huntsman Leopold","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"85":{"id":85,"t":"Lost Necklace","lv":6,"min":5,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Billy Maclure.","desc":"I lost my necklace, and think that guttersnipe Billy Maclure took it! He's usually scuttling like a rat around the Maclure vineyards east of here.\nGet my necklace back for me, and you'll warm an old widow's heart.","rew":"Experience: 140\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"You lost a what? Well I didn't take no necklace, because I ain't no thief!\nI might know who did but...<grin>...I'm too hungry to remember.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":34.5,"y":84.3,"n":"\"Auntie\" Bernice Stonefield","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":43.1,"y":85.7,"n":"Billy Maclure","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"8485":{"id":8485,"t":"The Brokering of Peace","lv":60,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Timbermaw Offering of Peace to Thrall in Orgrimmar.\nTimbermaw Offering of Peace\nReach 42000 reputation with Timbermaw Hold\nProvided: Timbermaw Offering of Peace","desc":"Your deeds go beyond the tale of a simple hero, ‹name›. If you are a representative of your people, then your people are ones we would work to make peace with.\nPlease - take this offering to the orcish warchief that resides in the lands of Durotar; I believe you call this city Orgrimmar. In times past, he had tried to make contact with us on behalf of his Horde. It is now only fitting to acknowledge you as the key in your Horde's efforts in brokering peace.","rew":"Experience: 9,950","back":"The warchief's greetings are bestowed upon you, ‹class›. Your deeds make the Horde grow stronger in these troubling times. Now, what business do you have with me?","done":"Indeed, this is a most fortuitous turn of events. Were a lasting peace to be made with these creatures, this would certainly give us an advantage in securing Kalimdor from external threats. I will notify the other leaders of the Horde of this immediately, and further diplomats will be dispatched!\nAs for you, ‹name›... you have shown courage in both diplomacy and in action. I thank you, as does the entirety of the Horde.\nFelwood Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":65.2,"y":2.7,"n":"Gorn One Eye","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.7,"y":37.8,"n":"Thrall","e":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"3125":{"id":3125,"t":"Faerie Dragon Muisek","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Sprite Darters or Sprite Dragons. Use the Muisek Vessel to shrink and capture the fallen Faerie Dragons.\n8 Faerie Dragon Muisek\nFaerie Dragon Muisek Vessel\nProvided: Faerie Dragon Muisek Vessel","desc":"‹name›, next I must have you capture a creature that in appearance, may look quite fragile, yet its powerful spirit is what we are truly after. The faerie dragons that I speak of have served the night elves as their allies. We must capture one so that the horde may benefit from this strength of spirit as well.\nHere is the muisek, ‹name›. Kill 8 sprite darters or sprite dragons, and capture their muisek. They may be found to the west of here.","rew":"Experience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Were you able to capture the muisek of the faerie dragons?","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Now the spiritual powers of the faerie dragon will be available to us.\nI hope you willing to perform another task for me.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":74.4,"y":43.4,"n":"Witch Doctor Uzer'i","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"3445":{"id":3445,"t":"The Sunken Temple","lv":51,"min":46,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Marvon Rivetseeker in Tanaris.","desc":"I have heard of a place that lies deep below the surface of the earth -- banished there by powers greater than I have ever seen.\nIf you wish to learn more of this place; the Sunken Temple, seek out a goblin named Marvon Rivetseeker. Much like Troyas and I, he has studied many ancient areas of the world. He was last known to have left his home in Ratchet to study the troll ruins in Tanaris.\nGood luck finding him; he hasn't been heard from in some time.","rew":"Experience: 3,650","done":"Yes, the Sunken Temple, I can say that I have seen it with my own eyes. Perhaps you'd like to hear more about it?\nYou look like the adventurous type -- I know things that may intrigue you...\nFeralas Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":31.8,"y":45.6,"n":"Angelas Moonbreeze","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":52.7,"y":45.9,"n":"Marvon Rivetseeker","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"565":{"id":565,"t":"Bartolo's Yeti Fur Cloak","lv":34,"min":29,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Bartolo Ginsetti of Southshore a Bolt of Wool, a Hillman's Cloak, Fine Thread and 10 clumps of Yeti Fur.\nBolt of Woolen Cloth Broken Tooth 2.4 % , Singer 0.5 % , Mirelow 0.2 % , Tattered Chest 0 % and 4 more\nFine Thread sold by Amy Davenport , sold by Gina MacGregor , sold by Gunder Thornbush , sold by Banalash and 4 more\nHillman's Cloak\n10 Yeti Fur Skhowl 30 % , Frostmaw 30 % , Giant Yeti 30 % , Ferocious Yeti 30 % and 2 more","desc":"I, the great Bartolo, shall make for you the world famous, Alliance renowned, Yeti Fur Cloak!\nTravel the planet and find yourself a better cloak, I dare you. Oh wait, what is that, little ‹race›? \"Bartolo, there is no finer cloak!\" Yes, yes! That, I have heard before.\nBartolo requires a Bolt of Wool, a Hillman's Cloak made by a skilled leatherworker, Fine Thread and Yeti Fur, of course! Bring to me these items and you shall be a happy customer!","rew":"You will receive:\nYeti Fur Cloak\nExperience: 2,700\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"So you have returned to the great Bartolo. Perhaps you have finished gathering the materials needed for your Yeti Fur Cloak? Or maybe you just enjoy basking in the greatness of me, Bartolo!","done":"Now it is time for the great Bartolo to work his magic! I require no wizard's staff, no mage's rod. For I, the great Bartolo, work magic with a mere needle and thread!\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":49.4,"y":55.5,"n":"Bartolo Ginsetti","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6085":{"id":6085,"t":"Taming the Beast","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use the Taming Rod to tame an Ice Claw Bear. Practice your skills, then return the Taming Rod to Grif Wildheart in Kharanos.\nTaming Rod\nProvided: Taming Rod","desc":"Perhaps you'd like a creature that possesses little more than brute strength. The ice claw bear is an excellent companion for a fledgling hunter like yourself, and can be found east of Kharanos. Here is the taming rod; try this animal as a pet and see if ya like it!\nWhen you return, I'll give ya the skills you will need to tame an animal of your choosing; this creature will face the challenges you face, and gain experience alongside you. I will also show you how to call it and dismiss it as ya like.","rew":"You will learn: Taming Lesson\nExperience: 850","back":"Have you tamed the ice claw bear yet?","done":"Here you are, ‹name›. I will now give ya the power to tame a beast, as well as call it and dismiss it as you please.\nFind yerself a good, loyal pet, and enjoy the hunt!","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":45.8,"y":53,"n":"Grif Wildheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"8645":{"id":8645,"t":"Obsidian the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Silverpine Forest","x":45,"y":41.1,"n":"Elder Obsidian","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"8725":{"id":8725,"t":"Riversong the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"The heavens, in their countless stars, hold answers to earthly mysteries, ‹name›. Might, then, the wise, and the lucky, gaze up and find truth?","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":34.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Elder Riversong","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9365":{"id":9365,"t":"A Thief's Reward","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 50.","rew":"You will receive:\nCrown of the Fire Festival\nExperience: 4,950","done":"You've proven yourself, today, ‹name›.\nWhile I have little else to give you, I do have this crown; a fitting gift for a conqueror. May it light your way.\nTeldrassil Dun Morogh Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.5,"y":92.2,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":61.3,"y":25.1,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50,"y":72,"n":"Festival Loremaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["midsummer"]},"6645":{"id":6645,"t":"Favor Amongst the Brotherhood, Core Leather","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Core Leather","back":"Many of the sacred recipes require the skin from Ragnaros' chosen pets.\nOffer 2 Core Leather, skinned from the smoldering corpses of the Core Hounds of the Molten Core and you shall be granted favor amongst the Brotherhood.","done":"Your offering has been accepted. Favor you have gained. Continue and you shall be allowed access to the ancient trades.\nStart Lokhtos Darkbargainer End Lokhtos Darkbargainer Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 6645","cats":["molten-core"]},"9045":{"id":9045,"t":"Redemption Headpiece","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make a Redemption Headpiece if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Headpiece, 15 Wartorn Plate Scraps, 5 Arcanite Bars and 2 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Headpiece\n15 Wartorn Plate Scrap Infectious Ghoul 22.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 21.6 % in Naxxramas , Plagued Deathhound 21.3 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 20.8 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n5 Arcanite Bar\n2 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"You will find the remnants of our fallen heroes on the corpses of the Lords of Naxxramas. Bring those desecrated keepsakes to me along with wartorn plate scraps and crafting materials capable of revitalizing the cursed armor and I shall craft a fine piece of armor for you.","rew":"You will receive:\nRedemption Headpiece\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"<Eligor points to his head.>\nKeep it covered, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.7,"y":48.6,"n":"Commander Eligor Dawnbringer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"91285":{"id":91285,"t":"Murlocs at the gates","lv":11,"min":7,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 8 Vile Fin Attackers and 8 Vile Fin Seers and report back to Breton Samuels when it is done.\nVile Fin Attacker slain : 0/ 8\nVile Fin Seer slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Normally we'd show our newcomers a bit more hospitality, but we've got a bit of a murloc problem at the moment.\nA tribe of murlocs used to use the keep as their spawning grounds. They've been a problem since we moved in and kicked them out, but now it's starting to get out of hand. You look like you've seen some action. Do you think you could help us drive back some of these pests? You'll find them lurking in the bluffs along the road to the east, and in the camps around the lake to the west.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSkullthumper Driftwood Smasher\nMoney: 4 0 gold, 4 silver, 0 copper Experience: 875\n+50 reputation with Undercity","done":"We appreciate the assistance. I'm sure this won't stop the attacks entirely, but it'll hopefully slow them down a bit. It's hard enough rebuilding this place without a murloc trying to stab you in the back with a spear.","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":21.8,"y":45.2,"n":"Breton Samuels","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"95125":{"id":95125,"t":"Otts masterwork","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Watch as Ott forges your blade.\nWatch Ott craft the blade","desc":"These are some truly fine materials, ‹class›. You honor me by allowing me to forge this blade for you and I only hope that I can live up to your expectations.\nPlease, stand back so that I may begin the forging process.","done":"This blade is my finest work and I hope it serves you well in your travels. Thank you again for this opportunity.\nAka'Magosh, friend.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":60.4,"y":26,"n":"Ott","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"4485":{"id":4485,"t":"The Tome of Nobility","lv":40,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Duthorian Rall in Stormwind.","desc":"Hello, ‹name›. I see your dedication remains strong, as does your faith.\nI think it is time you spoke with Duthorian Rall in Stormwind. There are some more lessons for you to learn, and I feel you are prepared.\nSeek him out in the Cathedral of Light, and ‹name›, take these lessons seriously. You've attained your status through humility and hard work, do not disappoint us by becoming arrogant.\nBe well.","rew":"Experience: 320","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":49.6,"y":49.8,"n":"Arthur the Faithful","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"3525":{"id":3525,"t":"Extinguishing the Idol","lv":37,"min":32,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort Belnistrasz to the Quilboar's idol in Razorfen Downs.\nProtect Belnistrasz while he performs the ritual to shut down the idol.","desc":"Near the entrance is an idol that functions as a macabre oven for the Quilboar; the beasts... they literally consume their abductees from the Barrens. I can shut down the idol and bind them from using it again, but I need your aid in doing so. My plan: escort me to the idol. Once we arrive, I'll commence the ritual. I'll barely be able to communicate with you, let alone defend myself. Protect me while I shut down the idol. If they take me down, then it's all over for us.\nAre you with me?!","rew":"You will receive:\nDragonclaw Ring\nExperience: 4,250","done":"Belnistrasz's sudden departure has left behind a burning brazier. As you stare in to the flame, the image of a great-winged red dragon fills your mind. A more graveled version of Belnistrasz's voice speaks directly to you.\n\"Indeed mortals, you are the heroes I had hoped you would be. Thanks to you the butchery these beasts were perpetrating is a thing of the past. My faith in mortals such as yourself has been once more renewed. Take this as a reward befitting of a hero.\"\nStart Belnistrasz Razorfen Downs End Belnistrasz Razorfen Downs , Belnistrasz's Brazier Razorfen Downs Level 37 , requires level 32 Difficulty 32 33 35 40 47 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 3525\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 37, 4,540 XP in all.\n1 [ 37 ] Scourge of the Downs\nIf you agree to aid Belnistrasz, speak with him again and hand the Oathstone he gave you back to him.\nBelnistrasz Razorfen Downs\n290 XP\n2 [ 37 ] Extinguishing the Idol this quest\nEscort Belnistrasz to the Quilboar's idol in Razorfen Downs. Protect Belnistrasz while he performs the ritual to shut down the idol.\nBelnistrasz Razorfen Downs\n4,250 XP","cats":["razorfen-downs"]},"7045":{"id":7045,"t":"A Smokywood Pastures Thank You!","lv":60,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from A Smokywood Pastures Thank You!.","obj":"Speak with Greatfather Winter in Ironforge.","desc":"We at Smokywood Pastures appreciate the recovery of the stolen treats, ‹name›. For that, we'd like to offer you a special gift... presented by none other than Greatfather Winter himself!\nPlease, speak with Greatfather Winter, and he will give you your Feast of Winter Veil gift from us here at Smokywood Pastures. From our farm to your plate, it's always Smokywood Pastures wholesome goodness... thanks to you, of course!","rew":"You will receive:\nSmokywood Pastures Special Gift\nExperience: 4,950\n+100 reputation with Steamwheedle Cartel","done":"Ho ho hello, adventurer!\nThe goblins told me that you have earned a special gift this holiday season, and I am pleased to give it to you. Here you go - have a wondrous Feast of Winter Veil this and every season in the future.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.5,"y":31.9,"n":"Wulmort Jinglepocket","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":56.4,"y":31.6,"n":"Greatfather Winter","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"1525":{"id":1525,"t":"Call of Fire","lv":12,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Fire Tar and 1 Reagent Pouch to Telf Joolam in Durotar.\nFire Tar Razormane Mystic , Razormane Geomancer , Razormane Thornweaver , Razormane Water Seeker\nReagent Pouch Burning Blade Cultist","desc":"But you did not come here for a history lesson, did you? You came for the Eternal Flame and fire totem.\nThe first step is to create a sapta and bind you to the flame.\nI can create the fire sapta for you if you bring me two items. The first is fire tar, a simple item usually carried by Razormane spellcasters in eastern Barrens.\nThe second item will be more dangerous: a reagent pouch from one of the cultists of the Burning Blade. You can find them in a cave above the ravines northeast of Razor Hill.","rew":"You will receive:\nFire Sapta\nExperience: 900","back":"I have enough ingredients for a sapta of fire if you can find the reagent pouch and some fire tar. The Burning Blade fanatics carry the proper components for most of their spells in those pouches, and usually have enough of the items I need that we will not have to search much farther for anything else.\nThe saptas are always made from ingredients that are closely tied to their respective elements. It makes our work easier because of the warlocks' ties to fire.","done":"These will do nicely, ‹name›.\nFire is more than chaos and destruction--do well to remember that. It is also about life, and creation. All things are tied together in such a way. Forces oppose one another, but at the same time, one cannot exist without the other. Both extinguish one another, but also give one another meaning. Always remember this.\nUsing different types of magic in conjunction with one another will show not only true skill, but great wisdom.\nDurotar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":38.6,"y":59,"n":"Telf Joolam","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"93125":{"id":93125,"t":"Going home","lv":43,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Maintain your reputation with the Gelkis, and escort Rokren out of the Outcast Hideaway. Then inform Nerlokh near the Valley of Bones about what happened.\nGelkis Clan Centaur\nEscort Rokren out of the Outcast Hideaway","desc":"You! I saw you outside fighting the outcasts. I know not where you come from, but I need your help.\nI was lured here by my Gelkis brethren with an assurance of safety. I knew the war in the Desolace was escalating beyond our control, but I never imagined my own people turning to necromancy in a convoluted bid to defect to the Magram clan. When I spoke out against this, they threatened to kill me if I ever stepped hoof outside this tent!\nPlease help.","rew":"Money: 45 0 gold, 45 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,700\n+500 reputation with Gelkis Clan Centaur\n0 reputation with Magram Clan Centaur\nLevel 43 , requires level 35 Difficulty 35 39 41 46 54 Side Both factions Quest ID 93125","cats":["shendralas"]},"1125":{"id":1125,"t":"The Spirits of Southwind","lv":55,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Free the spirits of 8 Tortured Druids and 8 Tortured Sentinels in Southwind Village, and then return to Layo Starstrike at the Valor's Rest graveyard of Silithus.\nTortured Druid slain : 0/ 8\nTortured Sentinel slain : 0/ 8","desc":"To our southwest lies a tragic site - the ruins of Southwind Village. This is where our work should begin, ‹name›.\nFrom what we've learned, this village was once a night elf base of operations for Silithus. It's long since overrun by the silithid hives that infest the wastes. I can only imagine the horror of the village's initial sundering...\nThe tortured spirits of fallen druids and sentinels wander the ruins aimlessly. Explore this locale, freeing the souls of these wretched beings as needed.","rew":"Experience: 5,650\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Alliance or Horde, it doesn't matter - no being deserves to be trapped on this world as a tortured spirit. The freeing of these souls will make things right, ‹name›.","done":"I had thought that maybe the huge swirling hive near the ruins of the village had played a part in its demise. It would seem that your work has proven this to be correct; the proximity of the hive poses a threat to any future work we may do here.\nI thank you for your benevolence in freeing the souls of the fallen; such work is never easy, I know. When you're ready, however, I'd like to ask for your assistance once more...","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":81.9,"y":18.9,"n":"Layo Starstrike","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8805":{"id":8805,"t":"Boots for the Guard","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Ornate Mithril Boots to Vish Kozus, Captain of the Guard at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing II in order to complete this quest.\n3 Ornate Mithril Boots\nLogistics Task Briefing II\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing II","desc":"The mounted division of the Cenarion Hold guard is in short supply of ornate mithril boots. Procure a batch and deliver them immediately to Captain Vish Kozus in Cenarion Hold.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":50.8,"y":33.7,"n":"Vish Kozus","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"3765":{"id":3765,"t":"The Corruption Abroad","lv":24,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Gershala Nightwhisper in Auberdine.","desc":"Stormwind -- such a bustling hub of activity.\nI have traveled from afar to seek help. Often it is heard that brave adventurers roam these city streets.\nMy brother, Gershala, requires assistance in Darkshore. He resides in the seaside town of Auberdine.\nThe journey is a long and epic one. It is for this reason that I ask the help of a seasoned ‹class› such as yourself.","rew":"Money: 13 0 gold, 13 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,450\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Ah, so my brother, Argos, sent you? I realize you must be weary from your travels. But we have much to talk about.\nStormwind City Darkshore","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":36.2,"y":67.6,"n":"Argos Nightwhisper","s":1},{"z":"Darkshore","x":38.3,"y":43,"n":"Gershala Nightwhisper","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"5125":{"id":5125,"t":"Aurius' Reckoning","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 9,950 experience instead of 8,850, 1.12 times as much.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nWill of the Martyr Blood of the Martyr\nExperience: 9,950","done":"‹name›, I am dying... but my soul is saved. For that, I owe you more than words can say. Please, take this... and fight on, brave ‹class›!\nStart Aurius Stratholme End Aurius Stratholme Level 60 , requires level 55 Difficulty 55 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Type Dungeon Shareable Yes Quest ID 5125\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 9,950 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] The Medallion of Faith\nAurius Stratholme\n2 [ 60 ] Aurius' Reckoning this quest\nAurius Stratholme\n9,950 XP","cats":["stratholme"]},"1445":{"id":1445,"t":"The Temple of Atal'Hakkar","lv":50,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Collect 20 Fetishes of Hakkar and bring them to Fel'Zerul in Stonard.\n20 Fetish of Hakkar Veyzhak the Cannibal 40 % , Atal'ai Warrior 40 % , Atal'ai Witch Doctor 40 % , Zekkis 40 % and 4 more","desc":"So he spoke of Jammal'an's prophecy?\nThe Atal'ai spiritual leader believes once Hakkar returns to Azeroth from the Nether, the god will grant the Atal'ai tribe immortality.\nFoolish trickery to bring about a premature doomsday if you ask me.\nBut you say the exile spoke of enchanted fetishes? This concerns me greatly. If these are in fact the key to the Atal'ai ritual which caused this mess, we must understand their intrinsic powers.\nVenture into the Temple, and seize the fetishes!","rew":"You will receive:\nGuardian Talisman\nExperience: 5,900\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"If the Atal'ai fetishes hold the power to summon Hakkar and fulfill Jammal'an's prophecy they must be seized. Such powers must be understood by the Horde!","done":"Brave ‹class›, you have proven yourself to be a great champion of the Horde.\nNow this collection of fetishes of Hakkar must be dealt with at once!","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":47.9,"y":54.8,"n":"Fel'zerul","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["sunken-temple"]},"5045":{"id":5045,"t":"Rising Spirit","lv":20,"min":14,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"4 Blood Shard Bristleback Geomancer 49 % , Bristleback Thornweaver 48.8 % , Bristleback Water Seeker 48.7 % , Bristleback Hunter 34 % and 4 more","rew":"You will learn: Rising Spirit","back":"Warriors of all types <snort> have need of a strong spirit. It drives you to greater feats when all hope has been lost. This is not unknown to the <snort> Razormane. We are a spiritual tribe--we are more proud of our connection to Agamaggan than our prowess <snort> in battle.\nBring me 4 blood shards and I will bless your spirit for battle. <snort>","done":"Our greatest warriors, and our greatest <snort> shamans would envy your will, ‹race›.\nDefeat more of the Bristlebacks knowing that they cannot stop you! <snort>","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.5,"y":59.3,"n":"Mangletooth","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"885":{"id":885,"t":"Washte Pawne","lv":25,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Washte Pawne's Feather to Jorn Skyseer at Camp Taurajo.\nWashte Pawne's Feather Washte Pawne\nProvided: Washte Pawne's Feather","desc":"The feather of Washte Pawne is painful to the touch.","rew":"Experience: 1,500\n+75 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"There is new resolve within you, ‹name›. A resolve born from pain...\nAre you burdened with the death of Washte Pawne?","done":"The thunderhawk is a rare beast of the Barrens, and its death can portend great fortune, or great doom.\nBut Washte Pawne, called Spirit Biter in Taurahe, can bring neither... or both.\nThe pain you felt from hunting Spirit Biter is the pang all feel who make great gains at great costs. The sting you felt is the pain of regret.\nBut I can see you have conquered this. You have learned that regret turns to wisdom, and that through pain one gains strength.\nYou have learned much, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":44.9,"y":59.1,"n":"Jorn Skyseer","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"485":{"id":485,"t":"Find OOX-09/HL!","lv":48,"min":43,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the distress beacon to Oglethorpe's homing robot at the head of the river in the Hinterlands, near Skulk Rock.\nOOX-09/HL Distress Beacon Hitah'ya the Keeper 1 % , Saltwater Snapjaw 1 % , Trained Razorbeak 1 % , Razorbeak Gryphon 1 % and 4 more\nProvided: OOX-09/HL Distress Beacon","desc":"You have uncovered some sort of strange, egg-shaped device made from metal. Fiddling with one of its knobs springs the egg to life, as it opens up into some sort of gnomish robotic contraption! A voice from inside the robotic egg crackles to life.\n\"My name's Oglethorpe Obnoticus, and my homing robot has crashed! I will reward you for its recovery; please take this beacon to the robot!\"\n\"I now have computed the coordinates of the robot for you; it crashed at the head of the river near Skulk Rock!\"","rew":"Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"You appear to have uncovered the wreckage of... a robotic chicken? The voice from within the egg crackles to life again:\n\"Yes, excellent work! This is indeed my homing robot, though my sensors indicate that it needs a jump start before it can fly back to Booty Bay for repairs. Go ahead and place the beacon inside the rover - the beacon will take care of the rest!\"","done":"You place the egg... distress beacon... inside the chicken... homing robot.\nHums and whirs are heard from inside the robot as it struggles to stand up. After the robot comes to life, Oglethorpe's voice is heard once more, but now from inside the robot:\n\"OOX-09/HL is working at least, but it needs major repairs! It is much too heavy for you to carry it... but I think I have an idea. Are you up for watching over it some more?\"","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":49.4,"y":37.7,"n":"Homing Robot OOX-09/HL","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"7845":{"id":7845,"t":"Kidnapped Elder Torntusk!","lv":51,"min":46,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Primal Torntusk at Revantusk Village in the Hinterlands wants you to rescue her mate, Elder Torntusk, from Jintha'alor.\nYou have been told that he is being held prisoner atop Jintha'alor, the Vilebranch capital city located in the southern region of the Hinterlands.","desc":"My mate was taken by Vilebranch savages in a bold midnight raid on our village. Our spies have told me that he is still alive and being held prisoner atop Jintha'alor. The Vile Priestess Hexx is said to be preparing him for a sacrifice to the faceless blood God, Hakkar.\nYou must save him, ‹name›! Our village could not stand a loss this great.","rew":"Experience: 4,900\n+150 reputation with Revantusk Trolls","done":"You must act quickly, ‹name›. Surely the guards have been alerted to your presence.","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":78.2,"y":81.2,"n":"Primal Torntusk","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":59.7,"y":77.8,"n":"Elder Torntusk","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"2965":{"id":2965,"t":"Portents of Uldum","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Nara Wildmane on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.","desc":"Ah, ‹name›, it is fortuitous that you have come to me again. Your revelations at the Uldaman dig site have certainly given us sages much discuss. I was doing just that with one of the druids, Nara Wildmane, when it dawned on me that her past adventuring experiences may have some great importance as to the next step we need to take.\nI would like for you to speak with her concerning her travels to the Valley of the Watchers in the Tanaris desert. She waits for you on the Elder Rise.","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"There is a place deep in the Tanaris desert called the Valley of the Watchers. The discs that you recovered... their translated glyphs make mention of a place called Uldum. Most think this place to be a myth.\nI know this to be false; Uldum exists. I've been there. Well... outside, at any rate.\nThe crux is this, ‹name›: we think there is a connection between the discs and Uldum, and we want you to go there.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":34.4,"y":46.9,"n":"Sage Truthseeker","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":75.6,"y":31.6,"n":"Nara Wildmane","e":1}],"cats":["thunder-bluff"]},"405":{"id":405,"t":"The Prodigal Lich","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Present Sevren's Orders to Bethor Iceshard in the Undercity.\nSevren's Orders\nProvided: Sevren's Orders","desc":"Bethor Iceshard, a high-ranking and powerful mage in the Undercity to the south, commands me to send him an agent with proven worth against the Scourge. You, ‹name›, will be that agent.\nPresent these orders to Bethor. He will then instruct you on your mission. I don't know its details, but it deals with recruiting a wayward Lich. And it will be dangerous.\nSo ready yourself, ‹class›. You must not fail.\nYou may find Bethor in the Magic Quarter of the Undercity.","rew":"Experience: 180\n+25 reputation with Undercity","back":"Greetings. Either you do not know who I am, or your business with me is urgent.\nBecause if neither of these were true, then you would not be foolish enough to disturb me...","done":"Ah, you are the agent sent by Magistrate Sevren. Then yes, your business with me is crucial.\nI trust Sevren has mustered someone suitable for my task...but we shall see.\nTirisfal Glades Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":61.3,"y":50.8,"n":"Magistrate Sevren","s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":84.1,"y":17.4,"n":"Bethor Iceshard","e":1}],"cats":["tirisfal-glades"]},"3845":{"id":3845,"t":"It's a Secret to Everybody","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Examine the items inside the pack and bring them to their owner.\nLarge Compass\nCurled Map Parchment\nLion-headed Key\nProvided: A Small Pack","desc":"Grabbing onto it, you pull the pack back to the shore. Perhaps if you examine the items inside the pack, you might find out more about who it belongs to.\nThere are a few stray travelers at Marshal's Refuge. Perhaps you might find out more there.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"Hi there. I've seen you before... Haven't I?","done":"Oh... Yes, these things do look familiar... well, kind of...","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":63.1,"y":69.1,"n":"A Small Pack","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":44.7,"y":8.1,"n":"Linken","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4245":{"id":4245,"t":"Chasing A-Me 01","lv":53,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Escort A-Me 01 back to Karna Remtravel in Un'Goro Crater.","desc":"Checking to see if you're prepared to lead A-Me 01 back to Karna Remtravel, you flip the switch to the \"Off\" position. Glancing around once again to make sure none of the gorillas are coming, you prepare to see what happens when you flip the switch back to the \"On\" position.\nThis is your last chance... are you sure this is what you want to do?","rew":"Money: 1 60 1 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,550","back":"Have you been able to help A-Me? That mithril casing you mentioned being destroyed was a good guess at what was wrong. I'm sure if you replace that, she'll reactivate and be able to come home.","done":"Oh, you've done it! Wonderful! Thank you, ‹name›.\nOh, my poor, A-Me. Look at all those dents. We'll get her up and running perfectly with just a little work.\nThank you again, ‹name›. I really appreciate it.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":67.7,"y":16.8,"n":"A-Me 01","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":46.4,"y":13.4,"n":"Karna Remtravel","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"4005":{"id":4005,"t":"Aquementas","lv":54,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Take the Book of Aquor, the Silvery Claws, and the Irontree Heart to Tanaris.\nUse the Book of Aquor to summon Aquementas.\nAfter you have the completed totem, take it to J.D. Collie in Marshal's Refuge.\nSilver Totem of Aquementas\nProvided: Eridan's Supplies","desc":"Take this bag of supplies with you to Tanaris. Travel to Lost Rigger Cove, and look for a circle of stones.\nThe eastmost peninsula is the secret...\nFrom this circle only, read from the book of Aquor; summon the only creature that can transform the items you collected into a totem to fight Blazerunner.\nAquementas will not be pleased to be awakened, but remember, you must remain in the circle for him to transform the items.","rew":"Experience: 5,450","back":"So you're back, eh? Hmm... Let me take a look at that, ‹name›.","done":"Blazerunner, you say...\nYes, I am aware that a strong elemental resides in the charred center of the crater. We all just keep our distance; none have been able to penetrate the powerful aura that surrounds him. Many have been pushed from the rocky paths onto the ground below when trying to face him.\nFelwood Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":51.3,"y":81.5,"n":"Eridan Bluewind","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":41.9,"y":2.7,"n":"J.D. Collie","e":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1685":{"id":1685,"t":"Gakin's Summons","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Report to Gakin the Darkbinder in the Mage Quarter of Stormwind.","desc":"Isn't that how it always works? Was looking for you all day and couldn't find you, now when I'm not expecting it, you come and walk right up to me.\nI've wasted enough time trying to find you, so I won't delay you any longer. Master Gakin's summoned you for additional training. Seems to me you should seek him out as soon as possible.\nYou'll find him in the basement of the Slaughtered Lamb tavern. By the way, you might want to keep that particular location quiet. Don't want word spreading about it.","rew":"Experience: 420","done":"I'm glad someone was able to get a hold of you, ‹name›. I was beginning to fear the worst. It would be a shame to lose you, after the time we've invested in you. We can talk later, though. Your training is the only important thing now.\nElwynn Forest Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.5,"y":66.3,"n":"Remen Marcot","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":39.2,"y":85.2,"n":"Gakin the Darkbinder","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4965":{"id":4965,"t":"Knowledge of the Orb of Orahil","lv":35,"min":35,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens.","desc":"Well, well, well... a pleasure to see you're growing in power, ‹name›. I'd wager you'd be about ready to speak to Menara Voidrender in the Barrens. If you haven't spoken to her before, then let me tell you, I don't think I've ever met another expert in the creation of items--orbs specifically--that can inprison even a demon to serve our will so easily.\nIf you're interested, she's in Strahad's tower above Ratchet in the Barrens.","rew":"Experience: 1,350","done":"Ah, you do seek something more... substantial. That I can help you if you truly are prepared.\nIt's a welcome change to see one of our kind seeking more power in forms other than just knowledge.\nSo, do you feel you're ready, ‹name›?\nDun Morogh The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":59.2,"y":22,"n":"Briarthorn","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"1845":{"id":1845,"t":"Brutal Helm","lv":30,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nBrutal Helm\nExperience: 1,850","done":"I give this helm to you.\nGreat deeds brought you to me, ‹name›, and Earthmother willing... even greater deeds lie before you.","pins":[{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":39,"y":56,"n":"Orm Stonehoof","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8405":{"id":8405,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.\nDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, ‹name›! For the Alliance!","rew":"Experience: 1,500\n+50 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Good work, ‹name›. Thanks to you, our natural defenses in Ashenvale will remain intact for another day.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"98245":{"id":98245,"t":"Razormaw needling","lv":29,"min":21,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 10 Razormaw Incisors for Howin Kindfeather.\n10 Razormaw Incisor","desc":"I don't know who I hate more: the bloody Dark Irons, the Dragonmaw, or the drakes they rode.\n<Howin spits.>\nI aim tae make things right. But we're gonna need some supplies.\nThese whelp scales will protect against dragonfire a good bit, but they're a pain in the arse tae weave together.\nThe Razormaw raptors up in Raptor Ridge to the northeast and Saltspray Glen to the northwest are so named for their pointy chompers--they oughta break through the scales.\nBring me a handful of the incisors.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":49.4,"y":42,"n":"Howin Kindfeather","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"4805":{"id":4805,"t":"Ice Thistle E'ko","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"3 Ice Thistle E'ko Ice Thistle Patriarch 20 % , Ice Thistle Matriarch 20 % , Ice Thistle Yeti 20 % , Rogue Ice Thistle 0.7 %","rew":"You will receive:\n3 Juju Escape","back":"In Winterspring, you will fight great creatures called da ice thistle yeti. These beasts move slowly, but dey are able to evade many blows from da protection their thick fur provides dem. If you wish ta gain da ability to dodge attacks, bring me da E'ko you find from dem.\nRememba, you must have the Cache of Mau'ari in your inventory if you want ta hunt for E'ko.","done":"Mau'ari can derive da juju for ‹name›... Use da Cache of Mau'ari to cast dis upon yourself or your allies.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":61.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Witch Doctor Mau'ari","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92645":{"id":92645,"t":"Breaking the breaker","lv":11,"min":6,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay Commander Belguilos in the Gustberry Lowlands.\nCommander Belguilos slain","desc":"This attack is going to be hard to repel unless we can take out the cult commander. Belguilos \"the Breaker\" they call her, and she's a veritable terror. She used to be a peacekeeper before the cult got out of control, and even then she was... off. As a cultist I can only imagine how much worse she could be now.\nI might just be sending you to your death, but someone needs to take Belguilos out if we are going to survive here. You can find her at the villa at the hill's base. Good luck, ‹class›.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nHunter's Cord Windsong Bangles Breaker's Gauntlets\nMoney: 3 0 gold, 3 silver, 0 copper Experience: 650\n+50 reputation with Windshapers\n+50 reputation with High Order","done":"Belguilos is dead? Four winds bless you, ‹class›.\nWe might just make it out of this alive after all.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":69.6,"y":67,"n":"Yorana Windyreed","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"94485":{"id":94485,"t":"Tears of the lady","lv":12,"min":8,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 8 Lady's Tear Moss.\n8 Lady's Tear Moss","desc":"If we are to save my fellows in the Nightclaw Den, I am going to need some ingredients for a poultice. The first and most important is a spindly moss called Lady's Tear. It typically grows on the base of the trees here in Shadowgale.\nThis moss secretes a sticky substance that acts as an antiseptic and is perfect for binding open wounds. I have gathered what little I can reach but I know there is more in this forest.\nGo and be swift. We are going to need a lot if the injured I left behind still live.","back":"Have you found the Lady's Tear?","done":"<Elegael takes the sticky mound of moss from you with a weak smile.>\nThank you, Trogdorp, you have done well. This is exactly what we need.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":61.6,"y":39.2,"n":"Elegael Thornpaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});